# Keeps the build context small and keeps host state out of the image.
#
# Both Dockerfile and Dockerfile.android do `COPY . .`, so without this the context ships
# node_modules, the Playwright reports, .git, and backend/alexithymia.db — a committed dev
# database — into a layer. docs/09-deployment.md §2 records this as an open build-hygiene
# issue for the frontend image; this file closes it for both.
#
# The Android build additionally regenerates android/ from the Capacitor template, so any
# local copy must not be copied in: a stale one would defeat the reproducibility the
# containerised build exists to provide.

node_modules
dist
dist-android
android
.gradle
.git
.github
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
backups
*.keystore
*.jks
local.properties

# Secrets. Compose reads .env on the host and passes only the named variables into the
# containers that need them; it never has to be inside an image, and an image layer is a
# thing that gets pushed to a registry.
.env
.env.*

# The backend has its own build context (./backend), so it is never needed in the
# frontend or Android image.
backend
